          "description": "Part-Time Xero Accounts Assistant (3 Days/Week) \n\nLocation: Remote | UK-based or UK hours preferred \n\nHours: 3 days per week \n\nStart date: Immediate \n\n \n\nAbout us \n\nWe're a UK-based events and hospitality technology company. We work with a broad range of clients across the UK and internationally, and we're looking for a reliable, detail-oriented accounts assistant to support our day-to-day financial operations. \n\nThe role \nThis is a part-time, ongoing freelance position covering two core areas: \n\n1. Xero reconciliations \nDaily/weekly bank reconciliations \nKeeping accounts clean and up to date \nFlagging discrepancies \n\n2. Debt chasing \nMonitoring outstanding invoices \nFollowing up with clients via email and phone \nMaintaining a clear record of chase activity and status \n\nWhat we're looking for \nProven hands-on experience with Xero (essential) \nSolid understanding of UK VAT – applying correct VAT charges and reconciling VAT transactions (essential) \nComfortable with client-facing debt chasing — professional but persistent \nOrganised, reliable, and able to work independently \nGood written communication skills \nStrong written and spoken English (essential) \nUK hours (essential) \n\nNice to have \nExperience in hospitality, events, or a similar SME environment \nFamiliarity with Stripe or similar payment platforms \n\nPlease include a brief note on your Xero experience and any debt chasing work you've done previously.",
