          "contractorTier": "INTERMEDIATE",
          "currency": "USD",
          "description": "We are a fast-growing hospitality distribution company specializing in premium food, beverage, wellness, and lifestyle products for luxury hotels, resorts, private clubs, and corporate clients throughout North America.\n\nOur company sources unique, emerging brands and manages everything from supplier relationships and pricing strategy to fulfillment and logistics. As we continue to grow, we're looking for an experienced Procurement & Pricing Manager to help build a scalable pricing process.\n\nThis is an opportunity to have a direct impact on our company's profitability and pricing strategy.\n\nAbout the Role\nWe are looking for someone with experience in hotel procurement, hospitality purchasing, foodservice distribution, or specialty food distribution who understands both supplier pricing and what hotel buyers are willing to pay.\n\nYour primary responsibility will be reviewing new products before they are added to our catalog and recommending competitive, profitable selling prices.\n\nThis role combines procurement analysis, pricing strategy, and market research.\n\nResponsibilities\nYou'll help us determine the optimal selling price for new products by evaluating:\nSupplier buy price\nFreight and landed cost\nManufacturer MSRP\nManufacturer website pricing\nWholesale marketplace pricing (Faire and similar platforms)\nCompetitive retail pricing\nHospitality market pricing\nComparable luxury hotel pricing\nMargin opportunities\nVolume pricing opportunities\nPricing consistency across product categories\nYou'll also:\nDevelop pricing recommendations that balance competitiveness and profitability\nCreate standardized pricing guidelines\nRecommend margin targets by product category\nIdentify opportunities to improve gross margins\nReview supplier pricing for accuracy\nAssist with vendor negotiations when appropriate\nBuild repeatable pricing processes for our operations team\nIdeal Background\nWe're looking for someone who has experience in one or more of the following:\nLuxury hotel procurement\nHotel purchasing\nHospitality sourcing\nFoodservice distribution\nSpecialty food distribution\nConsumer packaged goods (CPG)\nProcurement management\nCategory management\nPricing strategy\nSupply chain management\nExperience working with premium hospitality brands is highly preferred.\nPreferred Qualifications\nStrong understanding of wholesale pricing\nExperience evaluating landed costs\nKnowledge of supplier negotiations\nExperience building pricing models\nExcellent analytical skills\nAdvanced Excel or Google Sheets skills\nAbility to make recommendations backed by market data\nStrong attention to detail\nBonus if you've worked with:\nLuxury hotels\nBoutique hotels\nHospitality procurement companies\nFood distributors\nSpecialty grocery\nPremium consumer brands",
