          "contractorTier": "INTERMEDIATE",
          "currency": "USD",
          "description": "We are looking for a senior GoHighLevel expert who has already audited and fixed messy GHL accounts for agencies or service businesses.\n\nThis is not a beginner workflow setup job.\n\nWe need someone who can help us build and validate a professional GHL audit and fix process for client sub-accounts. The person must have real experience auditing existing GHL accounts, finding broken workflows, missed follow-up gaps, pipeline issues, bad tags, calendar problems, missed call text-back issues, reporting gaps, and then fixing them properly.\n\nWhat we need help with:\n\nGHL Account Audit Framework\n\nCreate a practical audit framework based on real GHL accounts you have audited before.\n\nThe audit should cover:\n\nworkflows and trigger logic\nforms and calendar triggers\nmissed call text-back\nSMS/email follow-up sequences\nno-response follow-ups\nno-show recovery\nappointment booking logic\nConversation AI setup, if applicable\npipeline stages and opportunity movement\ntags, custom fields, and smart lists\nlead source tracking\nduplicate contacts\nstale opportunities\nuser permissions\nreporting and dashboard gaps\nLC Phone/Twilio/SMS setup\ncompliance risks where relevant\naccount cleanup priorities\nSample Completed Audit Report\n\nWe need a polished sample audit report that shows how you would present findings to an agency or client.\n\nThe report should include:\n\nwhat was checked\nwhat issue was found\nscreenshot/example of the issue\nwhy it matters\nwhat sales or revenue risk it creates\npriority level\nrecommended fix\nestimated effort\nbefore/after notes where possible\n\nYou can use dummy data, redacted screenshots, or a test account. Do not share private client data.\n\nFix Plan / Cleanup SOP\n\nCreate a clear fix process for the most common GHL problems found during audits.\n\nThis should include:\n\nbroken workflow fix process\npipeline cleanup process\ntag cleanup process\ncalendar/reminder fix process\nmissed call and no-response recovery setup\nstale lead reactivation setup\nreporting/dashboard cleanup\ndocumentation and handoff process\nProof Pack\n\nWe are only interested in applicants who can show proof of real work.\n\nPlease include at least one of these:\n\nLoom walkthrough of a GHL account you audited or fixed\nredacted before/after screenshots\nredacted audit report\nworkflow screenshots\npipeline cleanup screenshots\nclient handoff document\ncase study showing what was broken and what you fixed\n\nPlease do not send generic GHL screenshots. We want proof that you have audited, diagnosed, and fixed existing accounts.\n\nLoom Walkthrough\n\nAfter creating the framework and sample report, record a Loom walkthrough explaining:\n\nhow to run the audit\nwhat to check first\nhow to identify high-risk issues\nhow to decide what to fix first\nhow to present findings to an agency/client\nhow to document fixes after implementation\n\nWho this is for:\n\nYou are a fit if you have:\n\ndeep hands-on GoHighLevel experience\nexperience auditing existing GHL accounts\nexperience fixing broken workflows and pipelines\nexperience with agencies or multi-sub-account setups\nstrong documentation habits\nability to explain your thinking clearly\nproof of previous audit or cleanup work\n\nYou are not a fit if:\n\nyou only build funnels\nyou only know basic workflows\nyou cannot show proof\nyou rely on generic AI-written audits\nyou have never cleaned up an existing GHL account\nyou cannot explain why a workflow or pipeline issue hurts sales follow-up\n\nDeliverables:\n\nGHL audit checklist\naudit scoring system\nsample completed audit report\nfix sprint SOP\nbefore/after change log template\nweekly proof report template\nDaily Revenue Queue template\nLoom walkthrough explaining the full audit and fix process\n\nTo apply, please answer:\n\nHow many GHL accounts have you personally audited or cleaned up?\nWhat is the messiest GHL account issue you have fixed?\nWhat are the first 10 things you check when leads are coming into GHL but sales are still slow?\nShare a Loom, screenshot, case study, or redacted audit/report that proves your work.\nHave you worked with agency sub-accounts or white-label GHL accounts before?\nWhat fixed price would you charge for this audit framework, sample report, fix SOP, and Loom walkthrough?\n\nImportant:\n\nAll communication must stay on Upwork. Please do not contact us outside Upwork.",
