          "description": "AI automation specialist (n8n/Make + LLM) for Shopify e-commerce - ongoing\n\nWe're an established Shopify e-commerce brand operating across 9+ markets, looking for an AI automation specialist to build and maintain our internal automations and the lightweight internal tools that sit on top of them.\n\nWhat the work involves:\nWe automate repetitive operational processes - product content generation and localization across markets, review handling, data syncing between tools, support routing, and ad-ops reporting. Some of these feed internal dashboards and tools that we host ourselves. Most run continuously at volume, so reliability, cost control, and clean error handling are important.\n\nStack and skills:\n1. Strong with n8n and/or Make, using Claude or OpenAI APIs as the intelligence layer inside workflows.\n2. Comfortable wiring MCP tools into workflows, and able to judge when a task should be a deterministic workflow versus an AI agent.\n3. Able to build and deploy lightweight internal dashboards/tools - e.g., pushing a React or static front-end from GitHub to Vercel and managing environment variables\n4. Some coding ability (JavaScript or Python) for custom nodes and edge cases.\n5. Real e-commerce experience required - ideally Shopify, with multi-market a strong plus. Familiarity with the Meta/Google APIs is welcome.\n\nHow we work:\nWe start with a small paid test task that mirrors real work, then move to an ongoing engagement if it's a good fit.\n\nTo be considered, please include in your reply:\n1. Links to 2–3 things you've actually shipped to production (not demo videos) - automations and, if you have them, internal tools/dashboards, e-commerce if possible.\n2. Which automation platform you default to, and why.\n3. A short outline of how you'd build a pipeline that pulls data from several sources, combines it, and feeds a dashboard you'd host.\n4. Your rate and your timezone / typical availability.\n\nLooking forward to seeing your work.",
