          "contractorTier": "INTERMEDIATE",
          "currency": "USD",
          "description": "We're a paid media agency specialising in hospitality, running paid social and Google PPC for a portfolio of restaurant and bar brands. \n\nAccurate conversion tracking is the backbone of how we report performance and optimise spend, so we want an experienced specialist to audit the setup for one of our clients.\n\nWhat we need\n\nA thorough, independent audit of our advert tracking and attribution setup across Google Tag Manager, Meta and Google Ads, with a clear, prioritised list of issues and fixes. We don't just want a \"looks fine\" rubber stamp - we want someone to genuinely stress-test the setup and find what's wrong.\n\n\nScope of work\n\nThere is no expectation to \"fix\" to create any changes in any of the platforms. This is an audit + advise task only. \n\nWe believe that our conversion tracking must not be accurate for this client, as the CPA is significantly lower than peers, so suspect we have a tracking issue.\n\nWe'd like the audit to cover:\n\nGoogle Tag Manager\n\nContainer hygiene: redundant, paused, or duplicate tags; broken triggers; orphaned variables\nTag firing order and timing issues\nDataLayer implementation and whether events are pushing the right values (transaction/booking value, IDs, etc.)\nConsent Mode v2 implementation and whether tags respect consent state correctly\n\n\nMeta Pixel\n\n\nPixel firing correctly on key events (Purchase/Booking), deduplication (event_id matching), and event match quality and importantly, whether reported conversions are accurate vs. inflated/duplicated\n\nGoogle Ads\n\n\nConversion actions setup, primary vs. secondary, dedupe, and attribution windows\nEnhanced Conversions configuration and coverage\nGA4 ↔ Google Ads import accuracy and any double-counting\n\n\nDeliverables\n\n\nA written audit report listing every issue found, prioritised by severity and impact (critical / important / nice-to-have)\n\nClear, specific recommended fixes for each issue - actionable enough for our team to implement, with implementation difficulty noted\n\nA short verification of which conversion events can be trusted today vs. which are unreliable\n(If templated/multi-account): a reusable audit checklist we can apply across other client accounts\n\nA 30–45 min call to walk us through findings\n\n\nNote: this is an audit and recommendations engagement, not implementation. We may engage separately for fixes.\n\n\n\nProject details\n\nFull client details and access will be provided upon contract commencement.",
